cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite the accompanying manuscript and
  the repository revision used in your work.
type: software
title: >-
  CCA microscopy: Code for Align Before You Segment
authors:
  - family-names: Lu
    given-names: Ruibo
    affiliation: >-
      School of Instrument Science and Technology,
      Xi'an Jiaotong University
repository-code: "https://github.com/ruibolu1103-arch/cca-microscopy"
url: "https://github.com/ruibolu1103-arch/cca-microscopy"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Research software for label-free cross-channel translation alignment
  in multi-channel fluorescence microscopy. CCA combines coarse
  correlation of frozen DINOv2 features with fine convolutional
  correlation and is evaluated as a front end to fixed segmenters.
  The accompanying manuscript is titled "Align Before You Segment:
  Label-Free Cross-Channel Alignment for Multi-Channel Fluorescence
  Microscopy" by Ruibo Lu.
keywords:
  - image registration
  - fluorescence microscopy
  - cross-channel alignment
  - cell segmentation
  - label-free learning
  - DINOv2
